# UI route correction05 — C author candidate

C is the implementation/test author, not an independent Gate reviewer. Only files under this candidate directory were written. Root products and frozen C19/Shared/UI01/02/03/04 artifacts remain untouched.

## Exact import boundary

Import the seven full products only after verifying each existing Root base SHA against manifest05. Six existing files use Root's actual04 bytes; `contract-route.spec.ts` is new and must not already exist. Original bytes are preserved under `bases/<relative-path>.bin`.

Root reported admin394/Native26 and lint/build23 passing for the previous source. Those results do not validate05. UI30 belongs to the previous candidate and is not final UI acceptance evidence. C did not execute Node, Angular, build, lint, tests, browser, HTTP, PG, Git, WSL, or environment tools.

## Route and response behavior

- ContractDetail subscribes to paramMap with distinct IDs and takeUntilDestroyed. A route change clears dialogs, form contents, old toasts, and the component-scoped store ACK/readback state before loading the new contract and approval. Leaving the component invalidates outstanding work.
- An immutable store scope token distinguishes A→B→A. Detail/approval reads also have independent request sequences, so an older same-contract read cannot replace a newer result. Loading/saving/finally updates are fenced too. Response contract IDs and approval target IDs must match the requested contract.
- The component filters both displayed contract and approval by the live route ID. Command methods use those filtered values and current readiness/loading state. A route change while a command is in flight prevents its later completion/error from closing the new page's dialogs or showing an old-page toast.
- Every managed draft retains a real “准备/重新准备合同条款” navigation entry. Existing prepared metadata no longer claims that the current core information is already ready. Actual payload_changed/source_changed failures keep the original server error and add an explicit signing-workspace recovery entry. This hint does not add a submit gate or retry a write.
- The actual POST ACK still returns to its originating caller. A stale scope cannot publish that ACK, initiate old-contract readback, or clear a newer command's saving state. A started04 readback uses private reads bound to its captured scope; it cannot reselect A after the route becomes B.
- B todo readback passes optional isCurrent to AuthStore.refreshTodos. A successful HTTP result is applied only while the scope/ACK/request remains current. Other auth callers retain the previous default and strict behavior; no unrelated auth flow changes.
- All retries remain reads. No automatic command retry, new route, RBAC change, financial page, upstream A authoring UI, client generation, or domain lifecycle change was introduced.

## Source tests — not executed

The existing04 source cases are retained. Seventeen new source cases cover:

- Seven store cases: late A detail/approval after B, old finally while B reads are pending, A→B→A identity, same-contract newest request, old A POST ACK while B writes, old started ACK readback after switching to B, and rejection of a write for a different selected scope.
- Nine real ContractDetail ComponentFixture + real ContractStore cases: same instance switches A→B despite a deliberately stale snapshot; late A detail/approval cannot replace B; B's actual submit request uses B/preparation-B/version; old approval cannot be acted on; dialogs/forms/ACK reset; old POST completion cannot close B's dialog or toast on B; old read failures are suppressed; mismatched returned contract IDs block writes; destroy stops param subscriptions; a draft PATCH retains the re-preparation entry; both payload_changed and source_changed retain the server failure and link to the actual selected-contract signing workspace without retry. The unrelated attachment child alone is omitted in this focused fixture; actual browser acceptance still includes it.
- One AuthStore case: a delayed todo result is ignored after the caller's scope changes, while the existing04 strict-failure/default-fallback/success cases remain.

The component fixture drains the SDK Subject doubles' promise callbacks before asserting the absence of stale UI effects. SDK fixtures use readable test IDs and are not real producer evidence.

## Root runtime observations still required

Use the same browser component instance to navigate /contracts/A→/contracts/B with A detail/approval deliberately delayed, then release A responses. Confirm URL, visible business number, preparation/review state, and every submitted action target all remain B. Repeat A→B→A, and route change while an A POST or ACK readback is pending. Confirm old ACK/error/toast/finally/todo responses do not replace B's state and that read-only retry never sends another write. Preserve previous failure records and rebuild assets before final UI acceptance.
